title: BasicSamples
---
<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Introductory Samples
SlideBullet: Welcome
SlideBullet: Yarn Basics
SlideBullet: Feature Tour
SlideBullet: Basic Saliency
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: We have four introductory samples

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Welcome
SlideImage: welcome
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: Welcome is this sample you are in right now.
Capsley: It doesn't show off any features
Capsley: It's a launching point for the entire samples package

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Yarn Basics
SlideBullet: Lines, options, variables and conditionals
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: Yarn Basics walks through the building blocks of a Yarn script, one step at a time

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Feature Tour
SlideImage: gauntlet
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: The feature tour shows off a wide range of [b]Yarn Spinner[/b] features
Capsley: If you want to get a quick look at what Yarn Spinner can do, check it out

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Basic Saliency
SlideImage: basic-saliency
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: Basic Saliency shows off the basics of using storylets
Capsley: If you aren't used to salient content in narrative, it's your best starting point
===

title: PresenterSamples
---
<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Presenter Samples
SlideBullet: Themed Line Presenter
SlideBullet: Phone Chat
SlideBullet: Options That Timeout
SlideBullet: Simple 3D
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: We have four samples on making and customising Presenters.

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Themed Line Presenter
SlideImage: rethemed
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: This sample shows off how with no code you can theme the existing dialogue system
Capsley: Is it really spelled "theming"?

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Phone Chat
SlideImage: phone
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: The phone chat shows off making an entirely new Presenter from scratch

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Options That Timeout
SlideImage: timeout
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: The time out options shows off how you can make timed player selection
Capsley: Where after a period of time an option is automatically selected

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Simple 3D
SlideBullet: Dialogue in a 3D scene
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: Simple 3D shows the built-in Presenters running in a 3D scene
===

title: ExtendingSamples
---
<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Extending Yarn Spinner
SlideBullet: Commands and Functions
SlideBullet: Instance Commands
SlideBullet: Voice Over
SlideBullet: Voice Over 3D
SlideBullet: Background Chatter
SlideBullet: Inline Events
SlideBullet: Replacement Markup
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: We have seven samples on extending [b]Yarn Spinner[/b] to create specific looks and feels

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Commands and Functions
SlideBullet: Instance Commands too
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: Commands and Functions shows how your Yarn scripts can call into your game, and ask it questions
Capsley: Instance Commands shows Commands that run on a particular node in your scene

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Voice Over
SlideImage: voiceover
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: The Voice Over sample shows off how to add in support for localisation and audio assets in your games
Capsley: Voice Over 3D does the same, with the voices coming from characters in a 3D scene

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Background Chatter
SlideImage: background
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: The Background Chatter sample demonstrates a variety of barks and background conversations
Capsley: Letting you create worlds that have conversations beyond that of just the player

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Inline Events
SlideImage: inline
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: Inline Events covers the new action markup and how it can be used to make actions occur in the middle of a line!

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Replacement Markup
SlideImage: replacement-markers
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: Replacement Markup shows off using the markup system to retheme and adjust partial elements of a line.
Capsley: This sample shows off using the built-in replacement markup systems as well as how to make custom ones.
===

title: AdvancedSamples
---
<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Custom Saliency Strategies
SlideImage: custom-saliency
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: This sample shows off how to make and use a custom saliency strategy
Capsley: Giving you full control over how dynamic content selection occurs

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Advanced Saliency
SlideImage: advanced-saliency
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: The Advanced Saliency sample demonstrates how you can use storylets and variables together to make dynamic content
Capsley: Where the characters, world, and scenario change depending on player selections

<<clear_slide>>
<<start_slide>>
SlideHeader: Node Internals
SlideImage: node-internals
<<end_slide>>

Capsley: The Node Internals sample demonstrates how to access the internals of nodes.
Capsley: Letting you query information that is otherwise not exposed through the default Yarn Spinner interfaces
===
